# device dumps, proprietary blobs and build outputs never belong in this repository
dumps/
firmware/
android-subset/
out/
*.img
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.bin
*.ko
busybox
tools/logdw/logdw
logs-*/
rootfs/base.tar
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
tools/bt-init/changxing60-bt-init
tools/gpu/cltest
# Same class as the two above: binaries we build ourselves from a source file that IS tracked.
# (tools/modem/changxing60-modemd.c + build.sh, and the modem-ioctl test helper.)
tools/modem/changxing60-modemd
tools/modem-ioctl
# The Chinese catalog we regenerate from tools/i18n/{zh-cn.json,build-i18n.py,lmo.py} (all tracked).
# The SHIPPING copy that build-rootfs.sh cp's into the image lives at
# openwrt/overlay/usr/lib/lua/luci/i18n/changxing60.zh-cn.lmo and IS tracked there (the overlay is
# mounted read-only in the build container, so it can't be regenerated at build time).
tools/i18n/changxing60.zh-cn.lmo
# Vendored third-party proxy cores, obtained from their upstream releases, not from this repo:
#   clash/bin/mihomo    -- the OpenClash core (clash/ is a vendored OpenClash tree; config.yaml IS tracked)
#   .../bin/sing-box    -- 86 MiB; container/build-rootfs.sh line 14 refuses to build without it and
#                          points at container/README for where to get it.
clash/bin/
container/overlay/opt/changxing60/bin/sing-box
# The vendored OpenClash web UI: a downloaded release, i.e. hashed Vite build output (note the
# dist/dist nesting) that nothing in this repo references. config.yaml next to it IS tracked.
clash/ui/dist/
work/
openwrt/*.tar.gz
upstream/stub/*.elf
upstream/stub/*.bin
kernel/merge.log
